      "entities": {},
      "text": "No. The problem lies not with terminological inclusivity per se but with the naturalization and reification of “cisness” through the expansion of its constitutive outside. Instead of being construed as cisgenderism’s inherent feature, all forms of gender nonconformity can now all be marked as aberrations that can be demarcated from cisgender normalcy. What results is a definition of “transgender” that marginalizes technologies of transitioning to preserve the supposed naturalness of the sexed body. It is this cleansing of cisness, rather than the expansion of transness, that works to obscure the fact that cis people have never existed."
